<title>UK: Brent Intl profit jumps after restructuring.</title>
<headline>Brent Intl profit jumps after restructuring.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		3.8		    vs 0.8</p>
<p> Shr pre-exceps	   4.4		    vs 1.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.0		    vs 0.6</p>
<p> Pretax		     5.28		   vs 2.01</p>
<p> Turnover		   71.51		  vs 71.43</p>
<p> Operating profit	 6.18		   vs 3.26</p>
<p> Exceptional loss	 0.41		   vs 0.37</p>
<p> Interest charge	  0.77		   vs 0.93</p>
<p> Tax			  1.90		   vs 1.04</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.38		   vs 0.98</p>
<p> Attributable	     2.84		   vs 0.44</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 25</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 22</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 14</p>
<p>NOTE - Inks to imaging management group Brent International Plc said it was increasingly confident that programmes it has initiated will deliver &quot;real and sustained improvements in shareholder value.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
